Early on focus on getting thrown daggers to Expert and increasing
AC.  Gradually build up around a dozen daggers for throwing then
gradually drop the lesser types one by one until you have a quiver
of a dozen stacked elven daggers.  That stack is the one to enchant
to high values.  Run away and barrage with broadside after broadside
of daggers thrown.

Do not avoid leveling up once you've gotten to the minetown altar as
spell casting improves with levels.  Since the first sacrafice gift is
Magicbane and some think that's the best artifact weapon for general
purposes, get that and never look back on the initial quaterstaff.

Somewhere in the range of the mines and sokoban it becomes
time to start switching armor items for ones that do not interfere
with spell casting.  Where the first body armor put on was probably
mithril, around the time of returning up from mines end it starts to
be a good idea to replace it with studded lether.  Conveniently your
pet will then be strong enough to take out the watchmen at this
point maybe even the watch captain.  Watchmen often have studded
leather armor.  Eventually the studded leather gets repaced by
dragon scale mail but all of the types of armor between those two
types interfere with spell casting.

After the quest late game wizards are killing machines.  Cast
various attack spells using thrown daggers as a backup, and some
powerful artifact weapon as a melee third or fourth fallback.  Get
to that point and then's when the danger is accident and typo.


